  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A disc of radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> and mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> is rotating in the horizontal plane at an angular velocity of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span> about its centre. Then a point mass of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2M\"></span> is dropped vertically onto the disc at a distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{2}\"></span> from the centre of the disc. The point mass sticks to the disc. The moment of inertia for the disc is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{1}{2}MR^{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the new angular velocity of the disc after the point mass has been dropped on it?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\omega}{8}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\omega}{4}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\omega}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\omega\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
